SVEthlana driver for FreeMiNT

The OpenCores 10/100 Mbps Ethernet MAC in the SuperVidel FPGA. Needs
SuperVidel firmware 10 or newer and SV_XBIOS.PRG (the packet buffers are
allocated in SuperVidel RAM through it).

The driver is a port of the Linux ethoc driver (drivers/net/ethernet/ethoc.c)
and of the part of the Linux PHY library the generic PHY driver uses. Names
are kept as in Linux so that fixes can be carried over. See the comments at
the top of svethlana.c for what was left out.

Installation

Copy svethlan.xif to the MiNT directory. The MAC address is read from
SVETHLAN.INF in the same place or in the root of the boot drive: twelve
hex digits, optionally separated by ':' or '-', for example

	00:20:43:58:78:3c

Without the file the driver keeps whatever the MAC registers hold, and if
that is not a valid address it makes up a locally administered one and
says so at boot. The address can also be set at any time with

	ifconfig en0 hwaddr 00:20:43:58:78:3c

The MAC has no EEPROM, so an address set this way lasts until the next
cold boot; put it in the network startup script or in SVETHLAN.INF.

Link state and negotiated speed/duplex are reported through the kernel's
alert channel when they change.
